nts": [{"type": "name", "content": "foundation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the basis or elemental structure of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When we start designing a model with these patterns, we'll have the foundation of the piece of software we want to develop."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "find a way "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to solve, find a solution or  disentangle something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: we have got to find a way to deal with physical architecture or hardware issues, if necessary."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tweaking "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "change, alteration or fixing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This application might not require too much tweaking for it to work on different hardware environments or dependencies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cohesion "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "well-connected, structured and logically organized  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We've got to focus on keeping cohesion between components, assign different interfaces to components, and what else?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Review information about how component diagram works."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a guideline for component diagram. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify key features of component diagram. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Collect the information and design a manual that helps you to understand component diagram process. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the manual to your instructor and partners"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collect useful information about component diagrams. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I understand how component diagrams work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I am creative when designing the manual. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain key features and guidelines related to component diagrams."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Time Clauses With When"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the future tense to talk about distant future or things that you haven't planned."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we have the foundation of the system in this model, we will then proceed to the high-level development stage, and even interfaces. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we have the software model defined, we'll address hardware."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to use the future tense, you can follow this structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <b>will + main verb (base form)</b> + complement.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Component diagrams <span class=\"strong\">will </span>become the most important way to develop business software.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to make negative sentences you can use the following structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <b>won't/will not + main verb (base form)</b> + complement.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Diagram icons  <span class=\"strong\">won't </span>disappear, but they'll adapt to developers' needs. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> future time clauses with when </span> to refer to something that will happen as a result of a possible action. In this case, you are joining a dependent clause to an independent one. You usually write the <span class=\"italic\"> dependent clause (when)</span> in <span class=\"strong\"> present, </span> and the <span class=\"italic\"> independent clause </span>in <span class=\"strong\"> future. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> I'll start using that diagram <span class=\"strong\">when </span>we reach an agreement.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can alternate the position of the clauses by separating them using a comma:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When </span>the project is finished, we won't discard the design. </span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Have Got"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">have got </span>to talk about obligations, necessity or possession."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to use <b>have got</b>, you need to take into account that this verb changes depending on the subject it follows, take a look at the following chart:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've got to take a look at the different diagrams that we can use for our next model. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've got to focus on keeping cohesion between components, assign different interfaces to components."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <b>have got </b>to express obligation or necessity by following the next structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> subject + <b>have got to /has got to + main verb (base form)</b> + complement</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">have got to use </span>component diagrams in this project. <br/>She <span class=\"strong\">has got to come </span>early tomorrow because she didn't finish creating that diagram.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Arthur</span>: We've got to take a look at the different diagrams that we can use for our next model. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Ennis</span>: I was thinking about the component diagram, but we've got to check if it's the most suitable. What do you think Arthur? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Arthur</span>: I know that component diagrams are an important part in model architecture because they show how components of a system connect to each other to create bigger components. When we start designing a model with these patterns, we'll have the foundation of the piece of software we want to develop.<br/>"}, {"time": "32000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Ennis</span>: Ok. We've got to take into account how this diagram works. Let me give you an example, this diagram has components that we can use to execute a stereotype function. We can wire these components together when we use an assembly connector; we have got to link this connector to what we call a lollipop and a socket symbol. Now, remember we have got to model components as rectangles, and when we have the foundation of the system in this model, we will proceed to the high-level development stage. We just need to work hand-in-hand. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Arthur</span>: That'd be both convenient and efficient for this project. But we also need to evaluate the limitations of component diagrams. I think that once we have the first stage or low-level development ready, we have got to find a way to deal with physical architecture or hardware issues, if necessary.\n<br/>"}, {"time": "96500", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Ennis</span>: But I think that in this stage we can use it, even though it is not widely used anymore. When we have the software model defined, we'll address hardware. The best we can do is start with the development of the basis for this software.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Arthur</span>: You're right! This application might not require too much tweaking for it to work on different hardware environments or dependencies. We've got to focus on keeping cohesion between components, assign different interfaces to components, and what else?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Ennis</span>: Hierarchies are quite important, we need to define different classes, how 